Contains Duplicate

Problem statement
Given array, return true if any number appears more than once

✅ Example:
nums = [1,2,3,1]
Output = true

✅ Best approach:
Use HashSet:
if number already exists in set → duplicate found

------------------------------------------------------------------
✅ Frequency Based

First Unique Character: find first character whose count = 1
Majority Element: element occurring > n/2 times
Top K Frequent Elements: most repeated numbers

✅ Grouping / Mapping
Group Anagrams: group words that are anagrams together
Example: ["eat","tea","tan","ate"]
→ [["eat","tea","ate"], ["tan"]]

✅ Prefix Sum + HashMap (Important for backend interviews)
Subarray Sum Equals K
Meaning: count subarrays whose sum = k
Example:
[1,2,3], k=3
Subarrays: [1,2], [3] → answer = 2

✅ Sliding Window + HashMap
Longest substring without repeating
Meaning: maximum length substring with all unique chars
Example: "abcabcbb" → "abc" length 3

Minimum Window Substring
Meaning: smallest substring containing all characters of another string
Example: "ADOBECODEBANC", "ABC" → "BANC"
